Definition <REF_0004>.\nApplying the functor (<REF_0005>) we obtain\n<MATH_0004>\nwhere <MATH_0005> denotes the finite dimensional <MATH_0006>-vector space\n<MATH_0007>. According to Lemma <REF_0006>\nthe condition of (S2) for <MATH_0008> also holds for this diagram.\nHence (S2) holds for <MATH_0009>.\n\n<STRUCT_0007><STRUCT_0008>\nPart (5) follows from the characterization of (RS) in\nLemma <REF_0007> part (2) and the fact that\n(<REF_0008>) commutes with fibre products.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7f66829834b975c0db2c946993f6e44ee46c9228fe04c115bdb3da59c0293a74", "unit_id": "tag:07WA:proof"}
